cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use q2sl attest, please cite it as below."
title: "q2sl attest: Quantum Syndrome and Source Limits"
abstract: >-
  Bounds what an observer can learn from the output of a quantum device. For a stabilizer code: the
  distance between the syndrome distributions of two logical states under noise that is not Pauli, its
  order in the noise strength, the attack an observer of the records achieves, and estimates from measured
  records. For a quantum random number generator: SP 800-90B min-entropy assessment, device attestation
  and extraction.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nikolas
    family-names: Klein
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NikoKleion/q2sl-Attest"
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - syndrome
  - side channel
  - amplitude damping
  - random number generation
  - min-entropy
  - stabilizer codes
